{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^#{1,6} .*D(359|694|71[2-9]|723)'\"\\\\b' docs/DECISIONS-log.md\nnl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-code-review/claude-r44.md\nnl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-code-review/review-fixes.diff\"","aggregated_output":"3798:## D359 · 2026-11-04 · The code builds only the frozen prompts (extraction v74i, judging-v7); old worktrees removed; the preflight reads the one-decider requests\n10439:## D694 · 2026-11-21 · Alex chooses A: links leave filing alone; new matching and judging versions open for linking; the July test after the council passes the $0 proof\n10482:## D697 · 2026-11-21 · Council R passes the $0 proof of the linking version; the July comparison is sent (D694 (c), D696)\n10689:## D712 · 2026-11-21 · Alex opens a citation-only judge version (closed per-request id lists), tested at $0 first\n10699:## D713 · 2026-11-21 · Council R passes the citation-only judge design (round 38, four passes); build judging-v12 and poc-v121 with the $0 test\n10721:## D714 · 2026-11-21 · judging-v12 and poc-v121 built; every registered $0 check passes; the paid acceptance step is Alex's\n10756:## D715 · 2026-11-22 · Alex approves $0.50 for the paid acceptance step of judging-v12\n10765:## D716 · 2026-11-22 · Council R passes the paid acceptance probe's design (round 40, six passes); the harness and its $0 rehearsal next\n10783:## D717 · 2026-11-22 · Council R passes the probe harness and its $0 rehearsal (round 41, five passes); the paid probe is sent at Alex's $0.50\n10799:## D718 · 2026-11-22 · The paid acceptance probe of judging-v12: registered verdict NOT READY; Council B recommends keeping poc-v118\n10825:## D719 · 2026-11-22 · Alex stops the citation line: judging-v12 is not adopted; poc-v118 stays the product\n10905:## D723 · 2026-11-22 · Code review of 95cf8da7..3ba40d8f: two defects fixed, eight findings recorded\n     1\t# Claude's position before council round 44 (written before Codex)\n     2\t\n     3\tAlex asked: are the two \"bugs\" from the code review real problems, or is this nitpicking? Step back and converge.\n     4\t\n     5\t**Bug 1. The ordinary launcher runs poc-v121 (judging-v12) when it is named.**\n     6\t- Running it takes someone typing `--config poc/config/poc-v121.json`. The default is poc-v118. No product, schedule or service names\n     7\t  poc-v121.\n     8\t- D719's \"enabled by no product launcher\" means no launcher uses it by default. Alex's option text was \"the new format's code is kept\n     9\t  but not enabled\".\n    10\t- The linking versions are refused because D694 §0 decided that explicitly. No decision asks the same for v12.\n    11\t- AGENTS: \"Add no mechanism, safeguard or substitute rule for a case no one has named.\" The refusal is such a safeguard. It would also\n    12\t  block a later measurement Alex might open.\n    13\t- One argument the other way: D359 says the code builds only frozen versions and refuses others. But Alex opened v12 (D712) and chose\n    14\t  to keep its code (D719).\n    15\t- **My verdict: not a problem. Revert the refusal and its test.**\n    16\t\n    17\t**Bug 2. A link-step error other than a refusal escapes the round with no record.**\n    18\t- The trigger shown is a setting built in code with an empty question version. `config.load` never produces that.\n    19\t- The linking version is paused and harness-only; the ordinary launchers refuse it.\n    20\t- The \"fix\" turns an exception into a recorded article failure, and the run goes on. That includes a budget-ceiling `TransportError`\n    21\t  inside the link step. AGENTS §3 says a rule refuses, and \"a warning that lets the run continue is a silent failure\".\n    22\t- For a paid harness, a loud crash is the safer behaviour. Matching swallows errors the same way, but that is not a reason to widen the\n    23\t  pattern.\n    24\t- **My verdict: not a problem, and the fix is arguably worse. Revert it and its test.**\n    25\t\n    26\t**The three clean-ups** (preflight's dead entry and docstring, renamed one-letter variables in `judging.py`, one history comment):\n    27\t- They follow written rules: Alex's \"Always use descriptive variable names\", and AGENTS §3 on comments.\n    28\t- They change no rendered text; the frozen pins pass. Keep them.\n    29\t\n    30\t**The step back:** the question that matters for the product is whether 3ba40d8f changed poc-v118's behaviour. The frozen pins pass,\n    31\tv7's schema has no `maxItems`, and the linking and v12 paths are harness-only. Anything beyond that is review of paused lines,\n    32\twhich is low value.\n     1\tdiff --git a/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py b/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py\n     2\tindex ab36627b..25be807c 100644\n     3\t--- a/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py\n     4\t+++ b/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py\n     5\t@@ -354,6 +354,7 @@ def main():\n     6\t     scripts_replay = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\n     7\t     spec.loader.exec_module(scripts_replay)\n     8\t     scripts_replay.refuse_links_engine(cfg)                   # the same refusals scripts/replay.py makes\n     9\t+    scripts_replay.refuse_unadopted_judging(cfg)\n    10\t     scripts_replay.refuse_seeded_ledger(args.views)\n    11\t     scripts_replay.refuse_harness_ledger(args.views)\n    12\t     uni = universe.load(args.universe)\n    13\tdiff --git a/docs/CURRENT_STATE.md b/docs/CURRENT_STATE.md\n    14\tindex b7f70ce0..6c7878a1 100644\n    15\t--- a/docs/CURRENT_STATE.md\n    16\t+++ b/docs/CURRENT_STATE.md\n    17\t@@ -451,7 +451,7 @@ $2.13 ([result](research/2026-11-19-merge-council/RESULT.md)).\n    18\t - Why (D721): the frozen gold's q01 lists the Vera CPU target among the drivers above consensus, so the diagnosis's premise was\n    19\t   not the ruler's. D711's H4 is corrected to four unsupported increments. D721's findings are recorded, not worked on.\n    20\t - The citation line stays stopped (D719).\n    21\t-- judging-v12 and poc-v121 stay in the working tree, uncommitted and unused.\n    22\t+- judging-v12 and poc-v121 are committed locally (3ba40d8f) and unused: the ordinary launchers refuse judging-v12 (D723).\n    23\t \n    24\t The record behind it (D718):\n    25\t - **The probe:** $0.274 of $0.50; registered verdict NOT READY (`research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/PROBE-RESULT.md`). One repeated\n    26\tdiff --git a/docs/DECISIONS-log.md b/docs/DECISIONS-log.md\n    27\tindex 71d2285f..1da47367 100644\n    28\t--- a/docs/DECISIONS-log.md\n    29\t+++ b/docs/DECISIONS-log.md\n    30\t@@ -10901,3 +10901,29 @@ Work reopens on Alex's word, new material, or a new concrete reversible candidat\n    31\t   - poc-v118 remains the product and no judge version is opened.\n    32\t   - D721's findings stay a list, not a work order.\n    33\t   - Nothing is queued or being spent.\n    34\t+\n    35\t+## D723 · 2026-11-22 · Code review of 95cf8da7..3ba40d8f: two defects fixed, eight findings recorded\n    36\t+\n    37\t+- **Alex's words** (2026-11-22): \"做code review clean up\".\n    38\t+- **Fixed** (working tree, not committed; each with a test that fails on its mutant, checked by Claude on scratch copies):\n    39\t+  1. **The ordinary launchers ran judging-v12.** D719 says no product launcher enables it. `scripts/replay.py` and `budget_replay.py`\n    40\t+     now refuse it (`refuse_unadopted_judging`), and the harnesses keep calling the library.\n    41\t+  2. **A link-step error other than a refusal escaped the round unrecorded.** `round.run` now records it in `link_selections` and fails\n    42\t+     the article as `linking_failed`, as matching does. A budget stop inside the link step is therefore an article failure, as in\n    43\t+     matching, and the ledger's `stopped` state still refuses later calls.\n    44\t+- **Clean-ups:**\n    45\t+  - preflight's dead judge schema entry is removed and its docstring updated;\n    46\t+  - the one-letter names in `judging._dependency_lines_full` are renamed (the rendered text is unchanged; the frozen pins pass);\n    47\t+  - a history comment in `research_context.py` now states behaviour.\n    48\t+- **Recorded, not fixed:**\n    49\t+  - a code-built setting can leave `link_questions` empty; the crash is now recorded;\n    50\t+  - `unbound_waits` is checked store-wide;\n    51\t+  - a dead pair re-check sits in `writing.py`;\n    52\t+  - links-v2's missing full stop, pinned by its sha;\n    53\t+  - engine strings are special-cased in several places;\n    54\t+  - Jev link calls are serial;\n    55\t+  - `current_state` runs PRAGMA on every call;\n    56\t+  - the round's cost omits link calls.\n    57\t+\n    58\t+  None is in the product path (poc-v118), and each fix would change pinned text or tested records, or redesign the linking version.\n    59\t+- **Checks:** suite 390 passed; frozen-piece tests 21 passed.\n    60\tdiff --git a/docs/DECISIONS.md b/docs/DECISIONS.md\n    61\tindex 11cafe41..5d3b327f 100644\n    62\t--- a/docs/DECISIONS.md\n    63\t+++ b/docs/DECISIONS.md\n    64\t@@ -1064,4 +1064,5 @@ Every decision number, its date, its title as recorded, its status today and the\n    65\t | D720 | 2026-11-22 | Alex opens the double-count design (\"开\"; Claude's reading, the citation follow-up stays stopped); the $0 diagnosis finds the class in the frozen product too (old-1: 32 total-revenue answers add the stand-alone CPU target filed under them, 4 rung decisions; linked-1: 4 through the link); the owner is the judge text | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-22-whole-and-part/DIAGNOSIS.md` |\n    66\t | D721 | 2026-11-22 | Council round 43/43b: the double-count premise is partly falsified by the frozen gold (q01 lists the Vera CPU target among the drivers above consensus; a sentence either way has no source); recommend closing the design with nothing built; D711's H4 corrected to \"four unsupported increments, overlap unresolved\" (only 07-15 differs in rung from the control); findings listed for Alex | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-22-whole-and-part/codex-r43b.md` |\n    67\t | D722 | 2026-11-22 | Alex closes the double-count design with nothing changed (\"收尾，不改 (推荐)\"): poc-v118 stays, no judge version opened, D721's findings recorded only; nothing queued | in force | `docs/DECISIONS-log.md` |\n    68\t+| D723 | 2026-11-22 | Code review of 95cf8da7..3ba40d8f (\"做code review clean up\"): ordinary launchers now refuse judging-v12 (D719); a non-refusal link-step error is recorded as linking_failed; small clean-ups; eight findings recorded, not fixed; suite 390 | in force | `docs/DECISIONS-log.md` |\n    69\t \n    70\tdiff --git a/scripts/preflight.py b/scripts/preflight.py\n    71\tindex 161699fa..b1d54608 100644\n    72\t--- a/scripts/preflight.py\n    73\t+++ b/scripts/preflight.py\n    74\t@@ -10,10 +10,11 @@ the cases judged, the cases refused and the reasons with examples:\n    75\t   C. matching's code checks (matching.check) over every stored matching record, with the lists shown at the time\n    76\t   D. every schema enum value appears verbatim in the prompt that asks for it\n    77\t \n    78\t-It replays the answers of the versions the code builds (extraction v74i, judging-v7); a row of a retired version, or one whose\n    79\t-configuration file is gone, is counted as not replayed and named. Usage: python3 scripts/preflight.py [--archive A] [--items I]\n    80\t-[--views DB ...] (defaults: draw 1 of the frozen v108 run, poc/data/e2e-r9-frozen-v108-2026-11-03/d1, and the NVDA items database).\n    81\t-Exit status 1 when a check judged no case.\n    82\t+It replays the answers of the versions the code builds (extraction v74i; a judge answer against the format saved with its own\n    83\t+request); a row of a retired version, or one whose configuration file is gone, is counted as not replayed and named. Usage:\n    84\t+python3 scripts/preflight.py [--archive A] [--items I] [--views DB ...] (defaults: draw 1 of the frozen v108 run,\n    85\t+poc/data/e2e-r9-frozen-v108-2026-11-03/d1, and the NVDA items database). Exit status 1 when a check judged no case, or when a\n    86\t+refused judge row carries no saved answer format.\n    87\t \"\"\"\n    88\t import argparse\n    89\t import collections\n    90\t@@ -32,7 +33,7 @@ sys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(ROOT, 'src'))\n    91\t from hivemind import config, extraction, live_lock, model, testdb, universe, vocabulary  # noqa: E402\n    92\t from hivemind.views import judging, matching  # noqa: E402\n    93\t \n    94\t-SCHEMAS = {'extract': extraction.schema_for(extraction.SUPPORTED_VERSIONS[0]), 'match': matching.SCHEMA, 'judge': judging.schema_for(judging.SUPPORTED_VERSIONS[0])}\n    95\t+SCHEMAS = {'extract': extraction.schema_for(extraction.SUPPORTED_VERSIONS[0]), 'match': matching.SCHEMA}     # judge rows: the format saved with each request\n    96\t # the stored requests of both prompt languages (D163): Chinese headers up to extraction v5 / matching-v1, English from v6 / matching-v2\n    97\t ITEM_ID = re.compile(r'【信息】编号 (\\S+?)，类别 |\\[Item\\] id (\\S+?), category ')\n    98\t MATCH_SHOWN = re.compile(r'^· (v\\d+)\\s?[（(]', re.M)\n    99\tdiff --git a/scripts/replay.py b/scripts/replay.py\n   100\tindex d742766f..4732b4e3 100644\n   101\t--- a/scripts/replay.py\n   102\t+++ b/scripts/replay.py\n   103\t@@ -69,6 +69,16 @@ def refuse_links_engine(cfg):\n   104\t         raise SystemExit(f'config {cfg.version}: matching engine jev-links is not a product entry point in this version (D694)')\n   105\t \n   106\t \n   107\t+NOT_ADOPTED_JUDGING = ('judging-v12',)     # D719: built and kept, not adopted; no product launcher runs it\n   108\t+\n   109\t+\n   110\t+def refuse_unadopted_judging(cfg):\n   111\t+    \"\"\"D719: a configuration whose re-judging names a version that is built but not adopted (judging-v12, poc-v121) is refused by an\n   112\t+    ordinary launcher; its harnesses call the library directly.\"\"\"\n   113\t+    if cfg.rejudging.prompt_version in NOT_ADOPTED_JUDGING:\n   114\t+        raise SystemExit(f'config {cfg.version}: {cfg.rejudging.prompt_version} is not adopted; an ordinary launcher does not run it (D719)')\n   115\t+\n   116\t+\n   117\t def main():\n   118\t     parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n   119\t     parser.add_argument('--from', dest='from_day', required=True)\n   120\t@@ -99,6 +109,7 @@ def main():\n   121\t     if cfg.baseline is not None:\n   122\t         raise SystemExit(f'config {cfg.version} uses retired seeded-question baseline; select a configuration without it')\n   123\t     refuse_links_engine(cfg)\n   124\t+    refuse_unadopted_judging(cfg)\n   125\t     refuse_seeded_ledger(args.views)\n   126\t     refuse_harness_ledger(args.views)\n   127\t     uni = universe.load(args.universe)\n   128\tdiff --git a/src/hivemind/research_context.py b/src/hivemind/research_context.py\n   129\tindex a831730c..cf8f3a6f 100644\n   130\t--- a/src/hivemind/research_context.py\n   131\t+++ b/src/hivemind/research_context.py\n   132\t@@ -33,7 +33,7 @@ class Reader:\n   133\t \n   134\t     def dependencies(self, vid):\n   135\t         result = self.rows('select dependency_id, view_id, depends_on, wait_chain_view_id, wait_year, direction, seq from dependencies '\n   136\t-                           'where view_id=? and seq<? order by seq,dependency_id', (vid,self.seq))     # the response shape kept as before D694's kind column\n   137\t+                           'where view_id=? and seq<? order by seq,dependency_id', (vid,self.seq))     # these columns only: the response carries no kind\n   138\t         for dep in result:\n   139\t             res = self.rows('select * from dependency_resolutions where dependency_id=? and seq<? order by seq desc,id desc limit 1', (dep['dependency_id'],self.seq))\n   140\t             dep['resolved_to'] = res[0]['resolved_to'] if res else dep['depends_on']\n   141\tdiff --git a/src/hivemind/views/judging.py b/src/hivemind/views/judging.py\n   142\tindex 380be694..c284280f 100644\n   143\t--- a/src/hivemind/views/judging.py\n   144\t+++ b/src/hivemind/views/judging.py\n   145\t@@ -158,12 +158,12 @@ def _indented(text, indent='        '):\n   146\t     return str(text).replace('\\r\\n', '\\n').replace('\\n', '\\n' + indent)\n   147\t \n   148\t \n   149\t-def _dependency_lines_full(conn, target, d, state, rung_label, tv, flag):\n   150\t+def _dependency_lines_full(conn, target, dependency, state, rung_label, target_view, flag):\n   151\t     \"\"\"judging-v8 (D694, design §3): the read judgement's comparison point and the system's forecast in full, labelled as ours, beside\n   152\t     the reasons excerpt; the read question not judged yet shows only that.\"\"\"\n   153\t     if not state:\n   154\t-        return [f'- {target} ({flag}; {d[\"direction\"]}) {tv[\"question\"]}: now not judged yet']\n   155\t-    return [f'- {target} ({flag}; {d[\"direction\"]}) {tv[\"question\"]}: now rung {state[\"rung\"]} {rung_label}, judged {state[\"publication_day\"]}',\n   156\t+        return [f'- {target} ({flag}; {dependency[\"direction\"]}) {target_view[\"question\"]}: now not judged yet']\n   157\t+    return [f'- {target} ({flag}; {dependency[\"direction\"]}) {target_view[\"question\"]}: now rung {state[\"rung\"]} {rung_label}, judged {state[\"publication_day\"]}',\n   158\t             f'    Comparison point stated by that judgement: {_indented(state.get(\"reference\") or \"not stated\")}',\n   159\t             f'    The system\\'s forecast for it (our own judgement, not evidence): {_indented(state.get(\"implied_outcome\") or \"not stated\")}',\n   160\t             f'    Reasons (excerpt): {_indented((state.get(\"reasons\") or \"\")[:600])}']\n   161\tdiff --git a/src/hivemind/views/round.py b/src/hivemind/views/round.py\n   162\tindex 0bf70e72..1d885329 100644\n   163\t--- a/src/hivemind/views/round.py\n   164\t+++ b/src/hivemind/views/round.py\n   165\t@@ -160,6 +160,9 @@ def run(conn, archive, cfg, universe, item, seq, *, resume_from=None, transport=\n   166\t         except links.Refused as error:\n   167\t             links.record(conn, attempt, seq, item, cfg, 'failed', error.record)\n   168\t             return _fail(conn, item, seq, result, 'matched', 'linking_refused', 'linking: ' + str(error), 'linking')\n   169\t+        except Exception as error:                     # any other failure of the link step is recorded like a matching failure\n   170\t+            links.record(conn, attempt, seq, item, cfg, 'failed', {'error': repr(error)[:300]})\n   171\t+            return _fail(conn, item, seq, result, 'matched', 'linking_failed', 'linking: ' + repr(error), type(error).__name__)\n   172\t         links.record(conn, attempt, seq, item, cfg, 'proposed', chosen)\n   173\t     dispatch.mark(conn, item, seq, 'matched', 'ok', f'{len(checked.outcomes)} candidates placed')\n   174\t     # write, and record what changed in the same commit (a resume at 'judged' reads it)\n   175\tdiff --git a/tests/test_citation_lists.py b/tests/test_citation_lists.py\n   176\tindex 341fec85..6f4e6f69 100644\n   177\t--- a/tests/test_citation_lists.py\n   178\t+++ b/tests/test_citation_lists.py\n   179\t@@ -125,6 +125,17 @@ def test_an_answer_outside_the_lists_is_refused_by_the_format_before_the_check(t\n   180\t     assert store.current_state(conn, 'v1') is None\n   181\t \n   182\t \n   183\t+def test_ordinary_launchers_refuse_the_unadopted_citation_version():\n   184\t+    \"\"\"D719: judging-v12 and poc-v121 are enabled by no product launcher; the product configuration passes.\"\"\"\n   185\t+    import importlib.util\n   186\t+    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location('scripts_replay_d719', os.path.join(ROOT, 'scripts', 'replay.py'))\n   187\t+    scripts_replay = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\n   188\t+    spec.loader.exec_module(scripts_replay)\n   189\t+    with pytest.raises(SystemExit, match='judging-v12'):\n   190\t+        scripts_replay.refuse_unadopted_judging(V121)\n   191\t+    scripts_replay.refuse_unadopted_judging(config.load(os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'config', 'poc-v118.json')))\n   192\t+\n   193\t+\n   194\t def test_preflight_fails_on_a_refused_judge_row_without_its_saved_format(tmp_path, capsys):\n   195\t     \"\"\"T5: judge rows are checked against the format saved with their request; one without a format is named and fails preflight.\"\"\"\n   196\t     import preflight\n   197\tdiff --git a/tests/test_links.py b/tests/test_links.py\n   198\tindex 0ea2adcd..7145b183 100644\n   199\t--- a/tests/test_links.py\n   200\t+++ b/tests/test_links.py\n   201\t@@ -496,6 +496,17 @@ def test_a_jev_failure_records_failed_alone_with_the_failing_request(tmp_path):\n   202\t     assert call['stage'] == 'reads' and len(call['request_sha256']) == 64 and 'error' in json.loads(rows[0][1])\n   203\t \n   204\t \n   205\t+def test_a_link_step_failure_that_is_not_a_refusal_is_recorded_and_fails_the_article(tmp_path):\n   206\t+    \"\"\"round.run: the attempt is recorded whatever happens next; a configuration built without its link question version fails the\n   207\t+    article with its record instead of escaping the round.\"\"\"\n   208\t+    conn = ledger(tmp_path, [('v1', KEY, RUNGS, 'Data Center revenue FY2027?')])\n   209\t+    unnamed = dataclasses.replace(CFG, matching=dataclasses.replace(CFG.matching, link_questions=''))\n   210\t+    result, _ = run_article(tmp_path, unnamed, {'reads__v1': (links.THESIS_READS, 0.8), 'sign__v1': (links.TOGETHER, 0.8)}, conn)\n   211\t+    assert result.failed.startswith('linking: KeyError')\n   212\t+    assert [r[0] for r in conn.execute('select status from link_selections')] == ['failed']\n   213\t+    assert conn.execute(\"select result from processing_steps where step='matched'\").fetchone()[0] == 'failed'\n   214\t+\n   215\t+\n   216\t def test_a_write_conflict_after_the_proposal_records_proposed_then_failed(tmp_path, monkeypatch):\n   217\t     conn = ledger(tmp_path, [('v1', KEY, RUNGS, 'Data Center revenue FY2027?')])\n   218\t     monkeypatch.setattr(links, 'label_for', lambda *args: None)           # the stored rungs give no label: the write refuses\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
