{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"awk 'NR>=3798&&NR<=3820 || NR>=10439&&NR<=10463 || NR>=10689&&NR<=10700 || NR>=10825&&NR<=10843 || NR>=10905&&NR<=10934 {print NR \\\":\\\" \"'$0}'\"' docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"3798:## D359 · 2026-11-04 · The code builds only the frozen prompts (extraction v74i, judging-v7); old worktrees removed; the preflight reads the one-decider requests\n3799:\n3800:- Alex, on Claude's list of the two open cleanup items (the old worktrees, and the code paths only retired prompt versions take, with the\n3801:  cost that old versions could then no longer be re-run, only read from their stored results): \"你看完你告诉我呀\", then \"ok\".\n3802:- **Worktrees.** Removed: `fix/thesis-admission-v11` (its 102 MB of data were five SQLite files whose contents equal `main`'s; only the\n3803:  header counters differed), `cleanup/sequential-requests` (685 MB, 244 files byte-identical to `main`'s `poc/data`), `feat/parallel-day`\n3804:  (two text changes `main` already holds, 94 MB of the 2026-10-25/26 test outputs) and `feat/thesis-admission-v12` (a writer fix `main`\n3805:  covers where it reads, the sealed-run decision carried as D358, its quality review carried to `docs/research/2026-10-28-quality-review/`).\n3806:  What was kept from each is in `/Users/lchingen/hivemind-backups/old-worktrees-2026-11-04/` (README there); the branches stay. Kept:\n3807:  `fix/extraction-quality-2026-10-28`, whose ignored folders hold the stored end-to-end runs (679 MB; v91, v92, v94, v95), the results\n3808:  any later comparison reads.\n3809:- **One path in the code.** `extraction.py` builds the v74i request only: the Chinese builder, the per-version schemas, field notes,\n3810:  paragraph accounts, the placement call's paths and every version gate are gone; `SUPPORTED_VERSIONS = ('v74i',)` and a configuration\n3811:  naming another version is refused before any request (`require_supported`). The answer checks are unchanged except what only retired\n3812:  versions used: a bare year is a calendar year, an unlinked statement stays for the handover's 'no home' drop, the admission check reads\n3813:  `settled_by` and the obligation horizon, a candidate cites only groups its answer declares. `placement.py` keeps the takes lines, the\n3814:  v74i filing rule and the candidate-id pattern; the separate placement call is gone. `views/judging.py` builds judging-v7 only (theme\n3815:  block, evidence in view, the reference) and refuses another version. The parallel runner and the stream no longer pass the never-shown\n3816:  groups. Matching, the Idea API and the store are unchanged.\n3817:- **Proof, at no cost.** The three draws of the frozen v108 run (D354) replayed through the code from their stored answers, every paid call\n3818:  refused: before the change and after it, all 3,031 requests built byte for byte the same (key order included), no request the archive\n3819:  could not answer, and all 23 tables of each replayed ledger equal to the stored ledger. Suite: 260 tests pass (289 before; the tests of\n3820:  retired versions left with them, the rest now run on `poc-v108`); the frozen-file tests, the UI tests and `docs/check.py` pass.\n10439:## D694 · 2026-11-21 · Alex chooses A: links leave filing alone; new matching and judging versions open for linking; the July test after the council passes the $0 proof\n10440:\n10441:- **Alex's words** (2026-11-21), replying to the three choices of D693: \"A\". The options were:\n10442:  - **A**, recommended: (a) a chosen reading link leaves evidence filing alone (D265 applies only to a stated hierarchy); (b) open new\n10443:    matching and judging versions for the shared mechanism (both opening orders; the first test accepts only the existing-reader /\n10444:    new-target case); (c) after the $0 proof has passed the council, the July comparison (old-2, 07-10 to 07-12, three linked and three\n10445:    control sequences, both questions fresh, pass rule `dependency-design/codex-r2.md` §7(b)), cap $0.15, estimate $0.06–0.07;\n10446:  - **B**, the code and the $0 proof only, asking again before the paid test;\n10447:  - **C**, not now.\n10448:- **Decided (Alex):** A. poc-v118 stays the product and the control; the linking version is a new configuration. The sourced-reference\n10449:  change is not opened (it returns after the July measurement, D693).\n10450:- **Next:** the $0 work of D693 in order (tables and request audit; the July control rebuilt by request identity and filing replayed;\n10451:  real checks and writer with fixed answers for both orders and the listed events; built requests inspected, rule frozen, cap set),\n10452:  then the council on the proof, then the send.\n10453:\n10454:## D695 · 2026-11-21 · Alex narrows the first linking version to number questions, one of them newly opened\n10455:\n10456:- **The question** (after council R round 4, `docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/codex-r4.md`, NOT READY: the\n10457:  design's blanket exclusion of theme links narrowed the agreed lifecycle, and the full scope — themes shown once with the link's\n10458:  direction, a theme reading an asset, closed events read as historical until a successor, two questions opened by one article — needs\n10459:  more design rounds): \"连题的第一版，范围要多大？\" Options: only number questions (recommended): link two five-rung number questions\n10460:  of the asset kind, one of them newly opened; themes already reach every asset question through the theme block (D191, D195);\n10461:  yes/no event questions and two questions opened by the same article wait for a later version. Or the agreed design in full.\n10462:- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-21): \"只连数字题 (推荐)\".\n10463:- **Decided (Alex):** the first linking version links only a newly opened number question and an open number question it was shown,\n10689:## D712 · 2026-11-21 · Alex opens a citation-only judge version (closed per-request id lists), tested at $0 first\n10690:\n10691:- **The question:** \"试点到此收尾（结论\"说不准\"，花了 1.70 美元）。发现了两个问题：一是模型常写出不在名单上的编号，回答因此被退回，这次对照组就是因为这个停下；二是新版本让\"总收入\"把 CPU 收入又加了一遍。下一步做哪个？\"\n10692:  Options: 开引用格式新版本 (recommended: every id field of the judge's answer takes a closed list built from the request; $0 check on\n10693:  stored data that accepted answers still pass and the bad ids are excluded; asking again before any paid test); 先设计重复计算的修法;\n10694:  先停在这里.\n10695:- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-21): \"开引用格式新版本 (推荐)\".\n10696:- **Scope:** a new judge version whose only change is the answer format's id fields (D711's recommendation). The link direction stays\n10697:  a separate design. Design, then council review, then build with tests and mutants, then the $0 test; any paid test asks Alex again.\n10698:\n10699:## D713 · 2026-11-21 · Council R passes the citation-only judge design (round 38, four passes); build judging-v12 and poc-v121 with the $0 test\n10700:\n10825:## D719 · 2026-11-22 · Alex stops the citation line: judging-v12 is not adopted; poc-v118 stays the product\n10826:\n10827:- **The question:** \"新的引用格式（每栏只能从名单里选编号）实测的正式结果是\"未就绪\"。它确实消除了编号写错导致的退回：48 个回答 0 次退回，原来是 17 次。但有一组对照里，它两次写\"彭博预测 3,930 亿\"，引的却是雅虎汇总的同一数字。这种\"机构名和引用对不上\"的毛病旧格式也有，目前样本太小，分不清新格式是否让它变多。下一步怎么做？\"\n10828:  Options:\n10829:  - 先停在这里 (recommended: poc-v118 stays; the new format's code is kept but not enabled; no further spend);\n10830:  - 设计一个后续测试;\n10831:  - 推翻结论、直接采用新格式 (not recommended).\n10832:- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-22): \"先停在这里 (推荐)\".\n10833:- **Effect:**\n10834:  - poc-v118 remains the product configuration.\n10835:  - judging-v12, poc-v121, the validator's `maxItems`, preflight's saved-format check and their tests stay in the working tree,\n10836:    uncommitted and enabled by no product launcher.\n10837:  - The link-direction design (D711) and the citation follow-up are not started. No further spend.\n10838:\n10839:## D720 · 2026-11-22 · Alex opens the double-count design; the diagnosis finds the class in the frozen product too\n10840:\n10841:- **The context:** Claude's report after D719 listed two items not started, each waiting for Alex: the design of the fix for the\n10842:  total revenue adding the CPU forecast again (D711, H4), and a citation follow-up.\n10843:- **Alex's words** (2026-11-22): \"开\".\n10905:## D723 · 2026-11-22 · Code review of 95cf8da7..3ba40d8f: two defects fixed, eight findings recorded\n10906:\n10907:- **Alex's words** (2026-11-22): \"做code review clean up\".\n10908:- **Fixed** (working tree, not committed; each with a test that fails on its mutant, checked by Claude on scratch copies):\n10909:  1. **The ordinary launchers ran judging-v12.** D719 says no product launcher enables it. `scripts/replay.py` and `budget_replay.py`\n10910:     now refuse it (`refuse_unadopted_judging`), and the harnesses keep calling the library.\n10911:  2. **A link-step error other than a refusal escaped the round unrecorded.** `round.run` now records it in `link_selections` and fails\n10912:     the article as `linking_failed`, as matching does. A budget stop inside the link step is therefore an article failure, as in\n10913:     matching, and the ledger's `stopped` state still refuses later calls.\n10914:- **Clean-ups:**\n10915:  - preflight's dead judge schema entry is removed and its docstring updated;\n10916:  - the one-letter names in `judging._dependency_lines_full` are renamed (the rendered text is unchanged; the frozen pins pass);\n10917:  - a history comment in `research_context.py` now states behaviour.\n10918:- **Recorded, not fixed:**\n10919:  - a code-built setting can leave `link_questions` empty; the crash is now recorded;\n10920:  - `unbound_waits` is checked store-wide;\n10921:  - a dead pair re-check sits in `writing.py`;\n10922:  - links-v2's missing full stop, pinned by its sha;\n10923:  - engine strings are special-cased in several places;\n10924:  - Jev link calls are serial;\n10925:  - `current_state` runs PRAGMA on every call;\n10926:  - the round's cost omits link calls.\n10927:\n10928:  None is in the product path (poc-v118), and each fix would change pinned text or tested records, or redesign the linking version.\n10929:- **Checks:** suite 390 passed; frozen-piece tests 21 passed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
