{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/views/judging.py | sed -n '110,136p;179,220p;285,319p'\nnl -ba scripts/show_views.py | sed -n '27,53p'\nnl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '10914,10928p'\nnl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-code-review/review-fixes.diff | sed -n '145,173p'\nrg -n 'parallel manifest|stale.*manifest|runtime changed|manifest rejects' tests/test_concurrency.py docs/DECISIONS-log.md | head -25\"","aggregated_output":"   110\t\n   111\tdef themes_in_force(conn, view_id):\n   112\t    \"\"\"The theme block of an asset thesis: every open theme thesis with a current state, with its rung label and whether a\n   113\t    changed conclusion was recorded after this thesis's last judgement. Empty for a theme thesis.\"\"\"\n   114\t    if store.view(conn, view_id)['object_kind'] == 'theme':\n   115\t        return []\n   116\t    last = store.current_state(conn, view_id)\n   117\t    out = []\n   118\t    for row in conn.execute(\"select view_id from views where object_kind='theme' order by view_id\"):\n   119\t        theme_id = row['view_id']\n   120\t        state = store.current_state(conn, theme_id)\n   121\t        if not state or not store.is_open(conn, theme_id):\n   122\t            continue\n   123\t        updated = bool(last) and bool(conn.execute('select 1 from judgements where view_id=? and changed=1 and judgement_id>? limit 1',\n   124\t                                                   (theme_id, last['judgement_id'])).fetchone())\n   125\t        rung = store.rungs_of(conn, theme_id)[state['rung'] - 1]\n   126\t        out.append({'view_id': theme_id, 'view': store.view(conn, theme_id), 'state': state, 'rung_label': rung['label'], 'updated': updated})\n   127\t    return out\n   128\t\n   129\t\n   130\tSTANCE_FIELDS = ['reference', 'implied_outcome']   # D260: what the market expects, and the figure or date the evidence implies\n   131\t\n   132\t\n   133\tclass JudgementRefused(Exception):\n   134\t    pass\n   135\t\n   136\t\n   179\t    for p in pieces:\n   180\t        src = p['sources'][0] if p['sources'] else {}\n   181\t        lines.append(f'- {p[\"evidence_id\"]} [{p[\"tier\"]}; {p[\"speaker\"]}; original source {p[\"original_who\"]} {p[\"original_day\"]}; from {src.get(\"input_id\")} {src.get(\"publication_day\")}] {p[\"one_line\"]}\\n    Quote: {p[\"quote\"][:400]}')\n   182\t        if p.get('replaced'):\n   183\t            lines.append(f'    It replaces {p[\"replaced\"][\"evidence_id\"]} ({p[\"replaced\"][\"original_day\"]}): {p[\"replaced\"][\"one_line\"]}')\n   184\t        if p.get('same_as'):\n   185\t            lines.append(f'    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as {\", \".join(p[\"same_as\"])}; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.')\n   186\t        if p.get('revises'):\n   187\t            lines.append(f'    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of {p[\"revises\"][\"evidence_id\"]} ({p[\"revises\"][\"original_day\"]}); both are in force: {p[\"revises\"][\"one_line\"]}')\n   188\t    if deps:\n   189\t        lines.append('\\n[Current conclusions of the theses it depends on]')\n   190\t        for d in deps:\n   191\t            target = d['resolved_to']\n   192\t            if not target:\n   193\t                lines.append(f'- the {d[\"wait_year\"]} thesis on chain {d[\"wait_chain_view_id\"]}: not yet created ({d[\"direction\"]})')\n   194\t                continue\n   195\t            tv = store.view(conn, target)\n   196\t            state = store.current_state(conn, target)\n   197\t            flag = 'historical only' if d['resolution'] == 'history_only' else ('closed' if not store.is_open(conn, target) else 'open')\n   198\t            rung_label = store.rungs_of(conn, target)[state['rung'] - 1]['label'] if state else 'not judged yet'\n   199\t            if full_dependencies:\n   200\t                lines.extend(_dependency_lines_full(conn, target, d, state, rung_label, tv, flag))\n   201\t                continue\n   202\t            lines.append(f'- {target} ({flag}; {d[\"direction\"]}) {tv[\"question\"]}: now rung {state[\"rung\"] if state else \"-\"} {rung_label}; reasons: {(state or {}).get(\"reasons\", \"\")[:600]}')\n   203\t    if themes:\n   204\t        lines.append(f'\\n[Themes in force, {len(themes)}]')\n   205\t        for theme in themes:\n   206\t            tv, state = theme['view'], theme['state']\n   207\t            mark = f'; {UPDATED_MARK}' if theme['updated'] else ''\n   208\t            lines.append(f'- {theme[\"view_id\"]} ({tv[\"object_id\"]}, due {tv[\"due_day\"]}) {tv[\"question\"]}: now rung {state[\"rung\"]} {theme[\"rung_label\"]}; '\n   209\t                         f'judged {state[\"publication_day\"]}{mark}; reasons: {(state[\"reasons\"] or \"\")[:THEME_REASONS_CHARS]}')\n   210\t    if last:\n   211\t        lines.append(f'\\n[Previous conclusion, for comparison only] rung {last[\"rung\"]}; reasons: {last[\"reasons\"][:800]}')\n   212\t    else:\n   213\t        lines.append('\\n[Previous conclusion] none: this is the first judgement, so changed must be true.')\n   214\t    lines.append('\\nAnswer per the JSON schema. cites may name only the evidence ids listed above; '\n   215\t                 + ('cites_views only the dependency thesis ids listed above' if deps else 'cites_views must be empty: this thesis depends on no other thesis')\n   216\t                 + ('; theme_pushes only the theme ids listed above; a theme id goes only in theme_pushes, never in cites or cites_views' if themes else '') + '.')\n   217\t    return lines\n   218\t\n   219\t\n   220\tdef build_prompt(conn, view_id, prompt_version):\n   285\t        errors.append(f'rung {data[\"rung\"]} outside 1..{len(rungs)}')\n   286\t    for cited in data['cites']:\n   287\t        if cited not in allowed:\n   288\t            errors.append(not_allowed(cited))\n   289\t    for cited in data['cites_views']:\n   290\t        if cited not in deps:\n   291\t            errors.append(f'{cited} is not a dependency of {view_id}')\n   292\t    for push in data['pushes']:\n   293\t        if push['evidence_id'] not in allowed:\n   294\t            errors.append(bad_push(push['evidence_id']))\n   295\t    for field in STANCE_FIELDS:\n   296\t        if not str(data.get(field) or '').strip():\n   297\t            errors.append(f'{field} is empty: state what the market expects and the figure or date the evidence implies')\n   298\t    last = store.current_state(conn, view_id)\n   299\t    if last is None and not data['changed']:\n   300\t        errors.append('first judgement must say changed')\n   301\t    if last is not None and last['rung'] != data['rung'] and not data['changed']:\n   302\t        errors.append(f'rung moved from {last[\"rung\"]} to {data[\"rung\"]} but changed is false')\n   303\t    return errors\n   304\t\n   305\t\n   306\tdef _record(conn, cfg, view_id, seq, item, answer):\n   307\t    data = vocabulary.judgement_answer(answer.data)\n   308\t    judgement_id = store.insert(conn, 'judgements', view_id=view_id, seq=seq, input_id=item['input_id'], rung=data['rung'],\n   309\t                                reasons=data['reasons'], cited_evidence_json=json.dumps(data['cites']), cited_views_json=json.dumps(data['cites_views']),\n   310\t                                pushes_json=json.dumps(data['pushes'], ensure_ascii=False), changed=1 if data['changed'] else 0,\n   311\t                                theme_pushes_json=json.dumps(data.get('theme_pushes', []), ensure_ascii=False),\n   312\t                                reference=data.get('reference'), implied_outcome=data.get('implied_outcome'),\n   313\t                                why_changed=data['why_changed'], config_checksum=cfg.checksum, call_id=answer.call_id,\n   314\t                                request_sha256=answer.request_sha256, publication_day=item['publication_day'])\n   315\t    conn.commit()\n   316\t    return {'view_id': view_id, 'judgement_id': judgement_id, 'rung': data['rung'], 'changed': data['changed'], 'cost': answer.cost_usd, 'cached': answer.cached}\n   317\t\n   318\t\n   319\tJUDGE_WORKERS = 32     # a day's round is up to 40 judgements of about 16 s each in two dependency levels (themes, then assets); 32 at a time makes a round about two calls long (2026-11-02)\n    27\t    if args.object:\n    28\t        views = [v for v in views if v['object_id'] == args.object]\n    29\t    print(f'{len(views)} views')\n    30\t    for v in views:\n    31\t        state = store.current_state(conn, v['view_id'])\n    32\t        rungs = store.rungs_of(conn, v['view_id'])\n    33\t        label = rungs[state['rung'] - 1]['label'] if state else '还没判'\n    34\t        print(f'\\n== {v[\"view_id\"]} [{\"开着\" if store.is_open(conn, v[\"view_id\"]) else \"关了\"}] {v[\"object_id\"]} · {v[\"kind\"]} · 看的是「{v[\"looks_at\"]}」 · {v[\"year\"] or \"\"} · 到期 {v[\"due_day\"]} · 来自 {v[\"created_from_input\"][:50]}')\n    35\t        print(f'   问：{v[\"question\"]}')\n    36\t        print('   梯子：' + ' | '.join(f'{r[\"position\"]} {r[\"label\"]}：{r[\"condition\"]}' for r in rungs))\n    37\t        print(f'   状态：第 {state[\"rung\"] if state else \"-\"} 格 {label}' + (f'；理由：{state[\"reasons\"][:400]}' if state else ''))\n    38\t        deps = store.dependencies_of(conn, v['view_id'])\n    39\t        if deps:\n    40\t            print('   依赖：' + '；'.join(f'{d[\"resolved_to\"] or (\"等 \" + str(d[\"wait_chain_view_id\"]) + \" 的 \" + str(d[\"wait_year\"]))}（{d[\"direction\"]}）' for d in deps))\n    41\t        history = conn.execute('select publication_day, rung, changed, substr(why_changed,1,80) from judgements where view_id=? order by judgement_id', (v['view_id'],)).fetchall()\n    42\t        if len(history) > 1:\n    43\t            print('   历史：' + ' → '.join(f'{h[0]} 第{h[1]}格{\"*\" if h[2] else \"\"}' for h in history))\n    44\t        pieces = store.evidence_in_force(conn, v['view_id'])\n    45\t        print(f'   证据 {len(pieces)} 条' + ('：' if args.evidence else ''))\n    46\t        if args.evidence:\n    47\t            for p in pieces:\n    48\t                src = p['sources'][0] if p['sources'] else {}\n    49\t                print(f'     - {p[\"evidence_id\"]} [{p[\"tier\"]}] {p[\"one_line\"][:140]}  ({src.get(\"publication_day\")} {str(src.get(\"input_id\"))[:40]})')\n    50\t    print('\\n== 处理记录')\n    51\t    for row in conn.execute(\"select input_id, step, result, reason from processing_steps where step in ('handed_over','merged') or result='failed' order by id\"):\n    52\t        print(f'   {row[\"result\"]:6s} {row[\"step\"]:11s} {row[\"input_id\"][:70]} {row[\"reason\"][:80]}')\n    53\t    pool = conn.execute('select kind, key, count(*) from review_pool_entries group by kind, key').fetchall()\n 10914\t- **Clean-ups:**\n 10915\t  - preflight's dead judge schema entry is removed and its docstring updated;\n 10916\t  - the one-letter names in `judging._dependency_lines_full` are renamed (the rendered text is unchanged; the frozen pins pass);\n 10917\t  - a history comment in `research_context.py` now states behaviour.\n 10918\t- **Recorded, not fixed:**\n 10919\t  - a code-built setting can leave `link_questions` empty; the crash is now recorded;\n 10920\t  - `unbound_waits` is checked store-wide;\n 10921\t  - a dead pair re-check sits in `writing.py`;\n 10922\t  - links-v2's missing full stop, pinned by its sha;\n 10923\t  - engine strings are special-cased in several places;\n 10924\t  - Jev link calls are serial;\n 10925\t  - `current_state` runs PRAGMA on every call;\n 10926\t  - the round's cost omits link calls.\n 10927\t\n 10928\t  None is in the product path (poc-v118), and each fix would change pinned text or tested records, or redesign the linking version.\n   145\t@@ -158,12 +158,12 @@ def _indented(text, indent='        '):\n   146\t     return str(text).replace('\\r\\n', '\\n').replace('\\n', '\\n' + indent)\n   147\t \n   148\t \n   149\t-def _dependency_lines_full(conn, target, d, state, rung_label, tv, flag):\n   150\t+def _dependency_lines_full(conn, target, dependency, state, rung_label, target_view, flag):\n   151\t     \"\"\"judging-v8 (D694, design §3): the read judgement's comparison point and the system's forecast in full, labelled as ours, beside\n   152\t     the reasons excerpt; the read question not judged yet shows only that.\"\"\"\n   153\t     if not state:\n   154\t-        return [f'- {target} ({flag}; {d[\"direction\"]}) {tv[\"question\"]}: now not judged yet']\n   155\t-    return [f'- {target} ({flag}; {d[\"direction\"]}) {tv[\"question\"]}: now rung {state[\"rung\"]} {rung_label}, judged {state[\"publication_day\"]}',\n   156\t+        return [f'- {target} ({flag}; {dependency[\"direction\"]}) {target_view[\"question\"]}: now not judged yet']\n   157\t+    return [f'- {target} ({flag}; {dependency[\"direction\"]}) {target_view[\"question\"]}: now rung {state[\"rung\"]} {rung_label}, judged {state[\"publication_day\"]}',\n   158\t             f'    Comparison point stated by that judgement: {_indented(state.get(\"reference\") or \"not stated\")}',\n   159\t             f'    The system\\'s forecast for it (our own judgement, not evidence): {_indented(state.get(\"implied_outcome\") or \"not stated\")}',\n   160\t             f'    Reasons (excerpt): {_indented((state.get(\"reasons\") or \"\")[:600])}']\n   161\tdiff --git a/src/hivemind/views/round.py b/src/hivemind/views/round.py\n   162\tindex 0bf70e72..1d885329 100644\n   163\t--- a/src/hivemind/views/round.py\n   164\t+++ b/src/hivemind/views/round.py\n   165\t@@ -160,6 +160,9 @@ def run(conn, archive, cfg, universe, item, seq, *, resume_from=None, transport=\n   166\t         except links.Refused as error:\n   167\t             links.record(conn, attempt, seq, item, cfg, 'failed', error.record)\n   168\t             return _fail(conn, item, seq, result, 'matched', 'linking_refused', 'linking: ' + str(error), 'linking')\n   169\t+        except Exception as error:                     # any other failure of the link step is recorded like a matching failure\n   170\t+            links.record(conn, attempt, seq, item, cfg, 'failed', {'error': repr(error)[:300]})\n   171\t+            return _fail(conn, item, seq, result, 'matched', 'linking_failed', 'linking: ' + repr(error), type(error).__name__)\n   172\t         links.record(conn, attempt, seq, item, cfg, 'proposed', chosen)\n   173\t     dispatch.mark(conn, item, seq, 'matched', 'ok', f'{len(checked.outcomes)} candidates placed')\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2462:- Code review before the push ([request](research/2026-10-26-e2e-parallel/review-2-request.txt), [Codex, read-only](research/2026-10-26-e2e-parallel/review-2.txt); no correctness defect in request identity, commit order, matching order or thread ownership). Fixed, each with a test that failed first: (1) a restart under `--max-items-per-day` counted only the remaining items, so it dispatched an item beyond the day's limit (serial) or was refused by the manifest (parallel); the items an earlier run of the day wrote now count toward the limit. (2) The study and test comparison read 12 of the ledger's 20 tables; one comparison (`proof.ledger_rows`) now reads every product table without row ids, call ids and wall-clock times, and recomparing every stored pair found them identical (D180's recorded day, the 16-worker recorded run, the product-entry live run, the six D181 cross-replays, D182's fifteen days: 5,805 rows), the D182 mutant differing in 16 tables. (3) The entry point is tested with no arguments on the default Jev configuration (16 and 8 workers, serial ledger; a mutant default is caught). (4) A stale sentence in the current state. Found by Claude: a manifest left by another ledger in the same folder refused a fresh ledger that had written nothing of that day; such a manifest is now replaced, and a ledger that has written part of the day still refuses a changed contract.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"PYTHONPATH=src python3 -B -c '\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport sqlite3\nimport subprocess\nfrom unittest.mock import patch\nfrom hivemind import config, parallel_day\nfrom hivemind.views import judging, store\nfrom types import SimpleNamespace\n\ndef snapshot(module, commit):\n    file = module.__file__.split('\\\\''/src/'\\\\'')[-1]\n    source = subprocess.check_output(['\\\\''/usr/bin/git'\\\\'', '\\\\''show'\\\\'', f'\\\\''{commit}:src/{file}'\\\\''], stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL)\n    namespace = dict(module.__dict__)\n    exec(compile(source, file, '\\\\''exec'\\\\''), namespace)\n    return namespace\n\nold_config = snapshot(config, '\\\\''95cf8da7'\\\\'')\nold_store = snapshot(store, '\\\\''95cf8da7'\\\\'')\nold_judging = snapshot(judging, '\\\\''95cf8da7'\\\\'')\nold_setting = old_config['\\\\''load'\\\\'']('\\\\''poc/config/poc-v118.json'\\\\'')\nnew_setting = config.load('\\\\''poc/config/poc-v118.json'\\\\'')\ncommon_universe = SimpleNamespace(version='\\\\''fixed'\\\\'')\nassert old_setting.checksum == new_setting.checksum\nassert parallel_day.environment_key(old_setting, common_universe) \"'!= parallel_day.environment_key(new_setting, common_universe)\nfile = Path('\"'\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/views.sqlite'\\\\'').resolve()\nwith sqlite3.connect(file.as_uri()+'\\\\''?mode=ro&immutable=1'\\\\'', uri=True) as conn:\n    conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\n    views = [r[0] for r in conn.execute('\\\\''select view_id from views'\\\\'')]\n    recent = {v: judging.build_prompt(conn, v, '\\\\''judging-v7'\\\\'') for v in views}\n    with patch.object(store, '\\\\''current_state'\\\\'', old_store['\\\\''current_state'\\\\'']):\n        prior = {v: old_judging['\\\\''build_prompt'\\\\''](conn, v, '\\\\''judging-v7'\\\\'') for v in views}\nassert recent == prior and views\nassert json.dumps(judging.schema_for('\\\\''judging-v7'\\\\'')) == json.dumps(old_judging['\\\\''schema_for'\\\\'']('\\\\''judging-v7'\\\\''))\nprint(f'\\\\''{len(views)} stored views: v7 prompt and schema equal; v118 file checksum equal but saved parallel config key differs'\\\\'')\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"PYTHONPATH=src python3 -B -c '\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport sqlite3\nimport subprocess\nfrom unittest.mock import patch\nfrom hivemind import config, parallel_day\nfrom hivemind.views import judging, store\nfrom types import SimpleNamespace\n\ndef snapshot(module, commit):\n    file = module.__file__.split('\\\\''/src/'\\\\'')[-1]\n    source = subprocess.check_output(['\\\\''/usr/bin/git'\\\\'', '\\\\''show'\\\\'', f'\\\\''{commit}:src/{file}'\\\\''], stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL)\n    namespace = dict(module.__dict__)\n    exec(compile(source, file, '\\\\''exec'\\\\''), namespace)\n    return namespace\n\nold_config = snapshot(config, '\\\\''95cf8da7'\\\\'')\nold_store = snapshot(store, '\\\\''95cf8da7'\\\\'')\nold_judging = snapshot(judging, '\\\\''95cf8da7'\\\\'')\nold_setting = old_config['\\\\''load'\\\\'']('\\\\''poc/config/poc-v118.json'\\\\'')\nnew_setting = config.load('\\\\''poc/config/poc-v118.json'\\\\'')\ncommon_universe = SimpleNamespace(version='\\\\''fixed'\\\\'')\nassert old_setting.checksum == new_setting.checksum\nassert parallel_day.environment_key(old_setting, common_universe) \"'!= parallel_day.environment_key(new_setting, common_universe)\nfile = Path('\"'\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/views.sqlite'\\\\'').resolve()\nwith sqlite3.connect(file.as_uri()+'\\\\''?mode=ro&immutable=1'\\\\'', uri=True) as conn:\n    conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\n    views = [r[0] for r in conn.execute('\\\\''select view_id from views'\\\\'')]\n    recent = {v: judging.build_prompt(conn, v, '\\\\''judging-v7'\\\\'') for v in views}\n    with patch.object(store, '\\\\''current_state'\\\\'', old_store['\\\\''current_state'\\\\'']):\n        prior = {v: old_judging['\\\\''build_prompt'\\\\''](conn, v, '\\\\''judging-v7'\\\\'') for v in views}\nassert recent == prior and views\nassert json.dumps(judging.schema_for('\\\\''judging-v7'\\\\'')) == json.dumps(old_judging['\\\\''schema_for'\\\\'']('\\\\''judging-v7'\\\\''))\nprint(f'\\\\''{len(views)} stored views: v7 prompt and schema equal; v118 file checksum equal but saved parallel config key differs'\\\\'')\n'\"","aggregated_output":"43 stored views: v7 prompt and schema equal; v118 file checksum equal but saved parallel config key differs\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"agent_message","text":"**Keep the launcher block, revert the broad exception catch, and keep all three clean-ups.**\n\n### 1. The two bugs\n\n- **Bug 1 — REAL, low exposure.** Before the fix, an operator who explicitly passed `--config poc/config/poc-v121.json` could run the shelved judge, spend money, and save its judgements through either ordinary launcher. The default is v118, so routine runs were unaffected. I read D719’s “enabled by no product launcher” as covering explicit selection too. The fix enforces that boundary and leaves the experiment harness available. [D719](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10825) · [Replay](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/replay.py:90) · [Budgeted replay](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py:349)\n- **Bug 2 — NOT A PROBLEM for the product or its named runs.** The review test manufactures an empty link-question setting in Python. Loading either supported linking configuration supplies or validates that setting. The catch adds a failure record for that artificial case, but the harness already stops on an unexpected exception. [Review test](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_links.py:499) · [Config loader](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/config.py:89) · [July harness](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/july_test.py:175)\n\nI reproduced a budget refusal in memory with and without the catch. Both recorded the same article failure and stopped the budget ledger. `links._ask` already converts the transport error to `links.Refused`, and replay stops on the failed article. Claude’s continuation claim is incorrect. [Budget transport](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py:293) · [Link call](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/links.py:213) · [Replay stop](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/replay.py:108)\n\n### 2. The eight recorded findings\n\n**None warrants a product fix.** The repeated `PRAGMA` in `current_state` does run on v118, contrary to D723’s blanket statement. It adds a database query per lookup. Its speed impact is unmeasured. [D723](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10918) · [State lookup](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/store.py:234)\n\n### 3. What `3ba40d8f` changes for v118\n\n- **Judging and filing.** The v7 prompt matched byte for byte on 43 stored views, and its answer format matched too. `maxItems` only applies when the format declares it. v118 still uses ordinary Jev matching and supplies no proposed links to the writer. [Judging](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:58) · [Validator](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/model.py:220) · [Round](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/round.py:153) · [Writer](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/writing.py:113)\n- **Storage and preflight.** Opening a writable database adds the link table and dependency column. Preflight now checks refused judge answers against their saved formats and exits if one is missing. All six refusals in the two archives I checked had the original v7 format. [Store](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/store.py:25) · [Preflight](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/preflight.py:68) · [Preflight exit](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/preflight.py:362)\n- **Upgrade and resume.** An unfinished parallel replay started before the upgrade will reject its saved progress after the upgrade. I confirmed that the same v118 file produces a different saved settings key. The runner also checks the code version. Finish any such replay on the version that started it. [Setting](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/config.py:43) · [Resume check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/parallel_day.py:68)\n\n### 4. Action\n\n- **Keep** the v12 refusal in both launchers and its test. **Revert** the broad link exception handler and its test. [Review diff](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-code-review/review-fixes.diff:99)\n- **Keep** the preflight cleanup, the descriptive variable names in `judging.py`, and the `research_context.py` comment. Add no code. [Clean-ups](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10914)\n\nThe review was read-only. Claude’s follow-up was blocked by login, so this is my recommendation after checking its written position."}}
